/-
# Dregg2.Verify.FloorRatchetBaseline — the grandfathered refuted-floor carriers.

GENERATED by `#floor_ratchet_emit` (see `Dregg2/Verify/FloorRatchet.lean`). Do not edit
by hand except to DELETE lines. Every row here is a declaration whose type takes a
hypothesis this tree PROVES FALSE at deployed BabyBear parameters, so the declaration
is VACUOUS. They are grandfathered because they cannot all be ported at once — this
file is the RATCHET, and its only healthy direction is SHORTER.

## A ROW IS A PAIR: `declaration.name ⊣ floor+floor+…`

The floor set is EVERY refuted floor the declaration assumes, sorted. It is part of the
KEY, not a comment: a name already listed here that presents a DIFFERENT floor set is a
FRESH carrier and a hard build error. Before 2026-08-01 the key was the NAME ALONE, which
made every row a blanket exemption over the whole refuted-floor set forever — a listed
declaration could be drained of `compressInjective` and acquire `Poseidon2SpongeCR` in one
commit, or be deleted and reintroduced as a different theorem, and stay green. An audit
measured 477 declarations binding the three StateCommit floors directly, 161 of which bind
a SECOND refuted floor as well.

⚑ A row with NO `⊣` is a LEGACY row, left from that name-only format. It still
grandfathers its name against any floor set — i.e. the hole is still open for that one
declaration. `#floor_ratchet_emit` upgrades every legacy row that is still a carrier; the
gate prints how many survive on every run and the healthy count is 0.

* REMOVING rows: mechanical. After a port, re-run the plain
`#floor_ratchet_emit "…"` — it emits `baseline ∩ current`, so it can only shrink.
* ADDING rows: requires `#floor_ratchet_emit!` and shows up as added lines in review.
An added row is a claim that a new theorem HAD to be built on a refuted floor.
-/
