/-- ⚑ THE HAND-PASTE TARGET for a DELIBERATE RAISE. When `#floor_ratchet` fails it prints
its violating names already formatted as lines for this array; pasting them here is how you
grandfather a declaration that genuinely cannot be ported yet.

It exists because the obvious recipe does not work. A failing gate means `Dregg2.lean` has
an elaboration error, and `lean` writes NO olean for a module that errors — so
`FloorRatchetEmit` (which does `import Dregg2`) cannot run at all, or, worse, runs against
a STALE `Dregg2.olean` left by the last green build and silently reports a surface that
predates your change. Pasting needs no environment and no build.

Every line added here is a claim, on the record and in the diff, that a new declaration had
to be built on a hypothesis this tree PROVES FALSE at deployed BabyBear parameters — i.e.
that it is knowingly VACUOUS. Say why in the commit message. The next shrink-emit folds
surviving entries into the chunks above and drops the ones that got ported. -/
def manual : Array String := #[]

/-- The grandfathered carriers. Only ever gets SHORTER. -/
def grandfathered : Array String :=
  c0 ++ c1 ++ c2 ++ c3 ++ c4 ++ c5 ++ c6 ++ c7 ++ c8 ++ c9 ++ c10 ++ c11 ++ manual

